Assuming small-signal analysis with \(V_{DD}\), \(V_{b1}\), and \(V_{b2}\) as AC ground (ideal bias sources), this is a **PMOS cascode stack** and the resistance seen at the bottom node is:

\[
R_{\text{out}}
= \frac{g_{m1}+g_{ds1}+g_{ds2}}{g_{ds1}g_{ds2}}
= r_{o1}+r_{o2}+g_{m1}r_{o1}r_{o2}
\]

So the usual high-gain approximation is:

\[
\boxed{R_{\text{out}} \approx g_{m1}r_{o1}r_{o2}}
\quad \text{if } g_{m1}r_{o1},\, g_{m1}r_{o2} \gg 1
\]

(If body effect is included for \(M_1\), replace \(g_{m1}\) by \(g_{m1}+g_{mb1}\).)
